Modified by the APICookbook project, 2026-11-09 (F0-F6). Summary of changes
(details in docs/adr/0024-apicookbook-fork.md):

Removed
- The terminal UI (src/decode/tui/) and the interactive REPL path of cli.py; prompt-toolkit.
- Kitaru recording and replay (src/decode/runtime/recording.py, evals/harness/kitaru_*.py,
  the `evals kitaru` commands, the KITARU_* settings, the Kitaru Worker task-input branch);
  kitaru and kitaru-pydantic-ai.
- `evals mine` (evals/harness/mine.py), whose Opik trace reader needs Kitaru's importer.
- The web_fetch tool (src/decode/tools/web.py); markdownify.
- Skills (src/decode/skills/, src/decode/tools/skills.py).
- Learning memory on exit (src/decode/memory/extract.py).
- The Modal headless app and the `decode remote` commands (src/decode/remote/).
- Course material not copied: assets/, tasks/, index.html, running_the_code/, .decode/skills/,
  importers/, evaluators/, scripts/, Makefile, uv.lock (regenerated).

Changed
- Added an "anthropic" LLM provider (Claude) and made it the default; Gemini, OpenRouter and
  Modal stay selectable but unused.
- pydantic-ai-slim pinned to 2.66.0 (was >=2.46,<2.47, the Kitaru adapter's cap).
- The event renderer moved from src/decode/tui/render.py to src/decode/render.py;
  InputIntent moved from src/decode/tui/app.py to src/decode/harness/queue.py.
- one_line() moved from runtime/recording.py to runtime/summary.py.
- The Docker backend can run the worker hardened for anonymous visitors (SANDBOX_DOCKER_RUNTIME,
  SANDBOX_DOCKER_NETWORK, SANDBOX_DOCKER_HARDENED; all off by default, keeping upstream's worker).
- The hardened worker runs as the uid that owns the Workspace (1001 on the sandbox host), not 1000.
- `decode run` and the runner pass a per-run BANCS_PROXY_URL (only the cookbook proxy's prefix is
  accepted), and `decode run --events-jsonl` logs each tool call and result through pydantic-ai's
  event_stream_handler; the agent loop itself is unchanged.
- The build agent's tool list adds the three BaNCS tools and keeps everything else.
- Pydantic-ai 2.66 sends a tool retry as ToolReturnPart(outcome="retried"), not RetryPromptPart;
  compaction and the tests were updated for it.
- Tests for removed modules deleted; affected tests updated.

Added
- src/decode/runner.py: a private HTTP runner that starts `decode run` per visitor task on the
  sandbox host, with a slot cap, a wall-clock limit and worker cleanup.
- sandbox/: the session image and the sandbox host's setup, verify and smoke-run scripts.
- src/decode/tools/bancs.py: three read-only tools (search_endpoints, get_endpoint, get_body_schema)
  that read the BaNCS spec through the run's proxy, and the BaNCS part of the system prompt: decline
  anything off-topic; answer API questions from the spec without running anything; for tasks, find
  real records instead of asking, call only url_templates get_endpoint returned, make writes (each is
  held for the visitor's approval), and finish only after the code has called the bank.
- The runner's events cursor (GET /runs/<id>/events?after=N) for the website's live view.

Left inert (removed with the generic eval cases in F5): the skills_dir and web_fetch_timeout_s
settings, sandbox.workspace.seed_skills (a no-op without a skills directory), the
skill_dispatch regression case, and the Modal sandbox backend (src/decode/sandbox/modal_backend.py).
